<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-primary mb-4">Common Causes of Swollen Cheek</h2>
</div>
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Dental Abscess</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Infection at the root tip of an upper or lower molar causes cheek swelling on the same side. The swelling may be firm or partially fluctuant. Requires root canal or extraction alongside antibiotics. <a href="dental-abscess-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Dental abscess treatment</a> covers this in detail.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Periodontal Infection</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Gum infection from advanced periodontal disease causes diffuse cheek swelling, gum tenderness, and tooth mobility. <a href="bacterial-mouth-infection-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Bacterial mouth infection</a> treatment covers this cause.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Salivary Gland Infection</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">The parotid or submandibular salivary gland can become infected or obstructed, causing acute cheek swelling that worsens with eating. Pus may drain from the gland opening inside the mouth.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Buccal Space Infection</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">An odontogenic (tooth-origin) infection spreading into the buccal space between the cheek and outer gum. Causes significant cheek swelling, often with trismus (difficulty opening the mouth). <a href="tooth-infection-swelling-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Tooth infection swelling</a> page has more details.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Buccal Cellulitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Bacterial skin infection of the cheek — causes redness, warmth, and diffuse swelling of the cheek skin. Treated with antibiotics; may need drainage if an abscess forms within. <a href="facial-cellulitis-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Facial cellulitis treatment</a> covers this.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Facial Trauma / Hematoma</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A blow to the cheek from injury causes soft tissue swelling and bruising. Severe trauma may involve cheekbone (zygomatic) fracture requiring surgical reduction. <a href="face-infection-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Face infection treatment</a> covers post-traumatic infection care.</p></div>
