</div>
<ul class="space-y-6">
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Antibiotic Therapy</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Oral or IV antibiotics for bacterial cheek infections. Amoxicillin-clavulanate for dental-origin swelling; clindamycin for penicillin-allergic patients. Antibiotics alone without source control are insufficient for dental causes.</p></li>
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Salivary Gland Management</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Increased fluid intake, gland massage, sialogogues (citrus to stimulate saliva), and antibiotics for salivary gland infections. Salivary stones may require removal.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 md:p-12 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant">
